# A test run has opened `statusText` on Object.prototype. Native code looks above the literal for each name that it lacks: `{ status, headers }` finds what was planted there, so the literal is made and the built-in reads it.
# `{ headers, statusText, status }` has the name itself, and `method`, which it lacks, is not opened: it is taken apart. The records are those of the twin, literal-of-options-is-taken-apart.ir, and one more: the last line.
